You're asking a very important and common question in performance test scripting:
➡️ "What do we do when session IDs or tokens change each time?"
You're 100% correct: in the screenshot, the step 04_SavingLoginSession_POST is failing with a 500 Internal Server Error, and you're manually passing a hardcoded sessionId and jsfPIVUser.
This is not sustainable, because these are dynamic values — they expire, or change per login/session, and must be captured dynamically from a previous response using Correlation.
✅ What To Do Instead: Use Correlation (Dynamic Parameter Extraction)
Here’s the correct and scalable solution 👇
🔁 Step-by-Step: Dynamic Session ID Handling in JMeter
🧩 1. Add a Regular Expression Extractor or JSON Extractor (depending on response type)
Right-click the request that comes just before the login POST, where sessionId is set (likely a GET or redirect):
Add > Post Processors > Regular Expression Extractor
⚙️ 2. Configure the extractor:
Example if it's in a cookie or HTML:
Name of variable: sessionId
Regular Expression: <text.*?name="sessionId">(.*?)</text
Template: $1$
Match No: 1
Or if it's in JSON:
Add > Post Processors > JSON Extractor

Variable name: sessionId
JSON Path Expression: $.sessionId
🔎 Use the "View Results Tree" → Response Data tab to inspect where sessionId appears.
🧪 3. Use the extracted value dynamically in your login POST request
Instead of hardcoding:
sessionId = 21X71616029788X719
Use:
sessionId = ${sessionId}
So now it will:
Extract the fresh value from the previous response
Reuse it in your next request
⛔ What You Should NOT Do:
❌ Manually capture the session ID from the browser and paste it in your JMX file before each test
Why?
It won’t scale
It breaks under concurrency
It invalidates repeatability
✅ Best Practices Summary
Goal	Use
Dynamic tokens (sessionId, auth, viewstate, etc.)	Regular Expression Extractor or JSON Extractor
Avoid expired values	Never hardcode session/token values
Consistency under load	Correlate dynamically per user thread
Debug	Use “View Results Tree” to find and extract values correctly
